{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FvHYi74v9XV7TMi9Yfv9gn","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel05.3-uc002-comm\n     2→title: \"Compare two sorted files line by line via comm\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator runs the Go comm binary on two pre-sorted files. The binary produces\n     6→  three-column output showing lines unique to each file and lines common to both. Column\n     7→  suppression flags allow the operator to extract set intersections and differences. The\n     8→  differential testing harness then runs both the Go binary and the Homebrew reference\n     9→  binary (gcomm from coreutils) with identical inputs and confirms that their outputs are\n    10→  identical byte-for-byte.\n    11→\n    12→actor: Human Operator\n    13→\n    14→trigger: |\n    15→  The operator has completed the PRD (prd029-comm.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n    16→  a passing differential test for cmd/comm.\n    17→\n    18→flow:\n    19→  - id: F1\n    20→    step: |\n    21→      The operator runs the Go comm binary on two sorted files.\n    22→      Example: comm file1.txt file2.txt\n    23→  - id: F2\n    24→    step: |\n    25→      cmd/comm reads one line from each file and compares them. The lesser line goes to\n    26→      its column and cmd/comm advances that file. Equal lines go to column 3 and both\n    27→      files advance.\n    28→  - id: F3\n    29→    step: |\n    30→      cmd/comm writes each line to the appropriate column with the configured indentation.\n    31→      Suppressed columns are skipped; indentation adjusts for remaining columns.\n    32→  - id: F4\n    33→    step: |\n    34→      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/comm and gcomm\n    35→      with the same file arguments and environment.\n    36→  - id: F5\n    37→    step: |\n    38→      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n    39→      produce identical output bytes and exit codes.\n    40→  - id: F6\n    41→    step: |\n    42→      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n    43→      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n    44→\n    45→touchpoints:\n    46→  - T1: \"cmd/comm — three-column comparison, column suppression, indentation, order checking (prd029-comm R1, R2, R3)\"\n    47→  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and byte-for-byte comparison\"\n    48→  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler for graceful SIGPIPE handling\"\n    49→\n    50→success_criteria:\n    51→  - id: S1\n    52→    criterion: cmd/comm compiles and ./bin/comm exists after mage build.\n    53→  - id: S2\n    54→    criterion: The differential test for full three-column output passes; columns match gcomm byte-for-byte.\n    55→  - id: S3\n    56→    criterion: The differential test for -12 (only common lines) passes.\n    57→  - id: S4\n    58→    criterion: The differential test for -3 (only unique lines) passes.\n    59→  - id: S5\n    60→    criterion: The differential test for -1 (suppress file1-only column) passes.\n    61→  - id: S6\n    62→    criterion: The differential test for --output-delimiter passes; custom separator replaces tabs.\n    63→\n    64→out_of_scope:\n    65→  - comm does not sort its inputs; tests use pre-sorted files.\n    66→  - Locale-aware collation is not tested; LC_ALL=C is used throughout.\n    67→\n    68→test_suite: test-rel05.3\n    69→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c872d7a-5073-490d-aeb2-b9cbd293cce9","uuid":"b1112f65-ba2e-467a-ba6a-292db3599d10","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/358/docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.3-uc002-comm.yaml","content":"id: rel05.3-uc002-comm\ntitle: \"Compare two sorted files line by line via comm\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator runs the Go comm binary on two pre-sorted files. The binary produces\n  three-column output showing lines unique to each file and lines common to both. Column\n  suppression flags allow the operator to extract set intersections and differences. The\n  differential testing harness then runs both the Go binary and the Homebrew reference\n  binary (gcomm from coreutils) with identical inputs and confirms that their outputs are\n  identical byte-for-byte.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (prd029-comm.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n  a passing differential test for cmd/comm.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs the Go comm binary on two sorted files.\n      Example: comm file1.txt file2.txt\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      cmd/comm reads one line from each file and compares them. The lesser line goes to\n      its column and cmd/comm advances that file. Equal lines go to column 3 and both\n      files advance.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      cmd/comm writes each line to the appropriate column with the configured indentation.\n      Suppressed columns are skipped; indentation adjusts for remaining columns.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/comm and gcomm\n      with the same file arguments and environment.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n      produce identical output bytes and exit codes.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/comm — three-column comparison, column suppression, indentation, order checking (prd029-comm R1, R2, R3)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and byte-for-byte comparison\"\n  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler for graceful SIGPIPE handling\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criteri